<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
     lineage-sdk device overlay for the Meizu M5s.

     config_deviceHardwareKeys is a bit field:
       1 Home, 2 Back, 4 Menu, 8 Assist, 16 AppSwitch, 32 Camera, 64 Volume.

     The M5s has ONE physical key on the front — the mBack/mTouch home button
     built into the Goodix fingerprint module — plus the volume rocker.  That
     is 1 (Home) + 64 (Volume) = 65.  This differs from the m5c, which has
     three capacitive keys and uses 71.

     FACT for the "one key" part: the stock keylayout set carried in this tree
     (configs/keylayout/) has mtk-kpd.kl and gf-keys.kl, and the 15.1 tree's
     own note reads "Physical mBack click is mtk-kpd key 102. Keep light Goodix
     touch as Back-only".
     HYPOTHESIS for the bit value: 65 has never been observed working on this
     handset — no forge image has ever booted on it.  If hardware keys behave
     wrongly on the first boot, this integer is the first knob.

     config_longPressOnHomeBehavior=2 is carried verbatim from the 15.1 tree
     (long-press Home -> Recents), and the name was verified to still exist in
     lineage-sdk/lineage/res/res/values in this tree.
-->
<resources>
    <integer name="config_deviceHardwareKeys">65</integer>
    <integer name="config_longPressOnHomeBehavior">2</integer>
</resources>
